Sval: text under a rotating or skewing transform moves smoothly

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2063377 (mozilla-central f9eecdfcaa04,
Firefox 156) with its crash fix, Bug 2072715 (c2e9eaa4922b, Firefox
158). Adapted: ESR 153's ps_text_run.glsl picks the snap bias in
get_snap_bias(), so the Mixed case goes there, and ESR's prim_store
has no snap code that matches on SubpixelDirection. The rasterizer and
packing logic is unchanged. The wrench reftest changes (regenerated
PNGs, fuzz values and a new reftest) are left out: ESR 153's references
differ from the ones the commit replaced. 2072715's rasterizer unit
tests are kept.
Bug 2005426 (Firefox 148) removed SubpixelDirection::Mixed, so a
rotated or skewed run rounded each glyph to a whole device pixel, and
under a transform that changes slightly each frame the letters popped a
pixel at a time. Mixed is restored, with the 16 quarter-pixel variants
packed into one atlas entry the shader indexes. 2063377 alone aborts on
a near-degenerate transform, whose 16-variant packed entry overflows
i32; 2072715 drops any rasterized glyph above 2048px a side.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 158.

